{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) about the key pattern or difference in NVD publication timeliness across CVE severity levels, based on the box plot data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('NVD Publication Delay by CVE Severity') }}' (Figure 9) displays box plots illustrating the distribution of days between vendor patch release and NVD publication, broken down by CVE severity level (Critical, High, Medium, Low).
Examine the provided data summary for this chart (which might include median, Q1, Q3 days for each severity).
Identify and describe the most significant finding regarding timeliness and severity. For example:
- Is there a clear trend, such as Critical CVEs being published faster (lower median days) by NVD compared to lower severities?
- Which severity level shows the widest variability (largest IQR) in its NVD publication delay?
- Are there notable outliers in publication delay for any specific severity level?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates about the relationship between NVD publication timeliness and CVE severity.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('days_to_nvd_by_severity_boxplots') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
